# Marketplace: work order via API (`y-mp-work-order`)

Use this rule when you need a **new work order** in **Marketplace testing** **without** driving the SPA. Prefer **curl or a short script** so runs stay fast and repeatable.

Scratch multipart bodies and any other throwaway files: **`cursor_workspace/`** per **y-mp-ai-temp** (never the repo root).

## Artifact location policy (required)

- For this workflow, store **all generated test/temp artifacts** under:
  - **``cursor_workspace/``**
- This includes:
  - multipart payload temp files
  - API response snapshots/dumps
  - ad-hoc helper outputs used for WO creation/testing
  - any run notes/reports produced alongside this workflow
- Do **not** write new generated artifacts to repo-root directories (for example `ai_tests/`, `docs/`, `scripts/`) unless the user explicitly asks.

## Configuration (required)

Read **only** from:

``.env.e2e.local` (repo root)`

- `source` it in a shell (or load with `python-dotenv` in a one-off script). **Do not** paste secrets, echo JWTs, or commit env changes unless the user asks.
- **Auth + API host**
  - **`MARKETPLACE_JWT`**: raw JWT or `Bearer …`; normalize to `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
  - **`VENDOROO_BASE_API_URL`**: if unset, derive from **`MARKETPLACE_URL`** (testing UI → `https://api-testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai`).
  - **Non-browser clients:** send a **browser-like `User-Agent`**, and set **`Origin`** + **`Referer`** to **`MARKETPLACE_URL`** (testing MP API returns **403** without `User-Agent` even with a valid JWT).
- **Work order payload**
  - **`CLIENT_ID`** (integer): `clientId` on the create DTO. If you only have **`CLIENT`** (name hint), resolve **`id`** via **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-client.mdc`** (`SearchByName` / `SearchWithPagination`) before creating the WO.
  - **`locationId` (integer):** resolve in this order:
    1. **`LOCATION_ID`** or **`MARKETPLACE_LOCATION_ID`** if set in **`.env.e2e.local`**.
    2. Else use **`LOCATION`** (label string in the same file) + **`CLIENT_ID`** and call the Marketplace Location APIs per **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-location.mdc`** — prefer **`GET …/api/Location/SearchLocations`** (`SearchText` = `LOCATION`, `ClientId` = `CLIENT_ID`, **`PageNumber=1`** if you pass pagination; **`PageNumber=0` causes 500** on testing). If search misses, use **`GET …/api/Location/GetByClientId?clientId=`** and pick the row whose **`name`** matches **`LOCATION`** (exact match preferred).
    3. Optionally persist the resolved id as **`MARKETPLACE_LOCATION_ID`** in **`.env.e2e.local`** for faster reruns (do not commit secrets).
  - **`MARKETPLACE_URL`:** used for **`Origin`** / **`Referer`** and the workspace URL after create.

**OpenAPI reference (schemas + routes):**  
[https://api-testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai/swagger/v1/swagger.json](https://api-testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai/swagger/v1/swagger.json) — see **`WorkOrderCreateDto`** under `components/schemas` and **`POST /api/WorkOrder`**. The live binding used by the SPA is the **multipart** body below (plain `application/json` on this path returns **500** in testing).

## Standard create: `POST /api/WorkOrder` (verified)

**Endpoint:** `{VENDOROO_BASE_API_URL}/api/WorkOrder`  
**Method:** `POST`  
**Content-Type:** `multipart/form-data; boundary=<boundary>`

**Body:** one form part named **`WorkOrder`** with **`Content-Type: application/json`** whose value is a JSON **`WorkOrderCreateDto`** (see Swagger). A minimal payload that succeeds against testing MP:

| JSON field | Value |
|------------|--------|
| `clientId` | From **`CLIENT_ID`** |
| `locationId` | From **`LOCATION_ID`** / **`MARKETPLACE_LOCATION_ID`**, or resolve **`LOCATION`** via **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-location.mdc`** |
| `description` | Short plain-text title/summary (string) |
| `scopeOfWorkSummary` | HTML string for the issue body (e.g. `<p>…</p>`); backend appends “Created through / Created by” blocks |
| `sendUpdateToChatMessages` | `false` (required by schema) |
| `woNumberType` | `"autoNumbering"` |
| `recurring` | `false` |
| `startSyncout` | `false` |

Optional part **`Documents`**: binary file uploads (same as Swagger); omit if none. For **HTTPS image URLs** used in RabbitMQ / Roo payloads (fetchable by the service), upload to S3 per **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-upload-photo.mdc`** instead of inventing hosts.

**Response:** `200` with `data` containing at least **`jobToken`** (UUID), **`woNumber`**, **`clientId`**, **`locationId`**, **`clientName`**, **`scopeOfWorkSummary`**, status **Triage**, etc.

### `curl` shape (placeholders)

```bash
set -a && source `.env.e2e.local` (repo root) && set +a
AI_TEMP="`cursor_workspace/`marketplace"
mkdir -p "$AI_TEMP"
API="${VENDOROO_BASE_API_URL:-https://api-testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai}"
ORIGIN="${MARKETPLACE_URL:-https://testing-marketplace.vendoroo.ai}"
TOKEN="${MARKETPLACE_JWT:?set MARKETPLACE_JWT}"
case "$TOKEN" in Bearer*) ;; *) TOKEN="Bearer ${TOKEN#Bearer }";; esac
BOUNDARY="----cursorMpWo$(openssl rand -hex 8)"
WO_JSON=$(jq -nc \
  --argjson cid "$CLIENT_ID" \
  --argjson lid "${LOCATION_ID:-${MARKETPLACE_LOCATION_ID:?set LOCATION_ID, MARKETPLACE_LOCATION_ID, or resolve LOCATION via y-mp-location APIs}}" \
  --arg title "API maintenance check" \
  --arg html "<p>Automated API WO — issue description body.</p>" \
  '{clientId:$cid,locationId:$lid,description:$title,scopeOfWorkSummary:$html,sendUpdateToChatMessages:false,woNumberType:"autoNumbering",recurring:false,startSyncout:false}')
TMP=$(mktemp "$AI_TEMP/wo-multipart.XXXXXX")
{
  printf -- "--%s\r\n" "$BOUNDARY"
  printf 'Content-Disposition: form-data; name="WorkOrder"\r\nContent-Type: application/json\r\n\r\n'
  printf '%s' "$WO_JSON"
  printf '\r\n--%s--\r\n' "$BOUNDARY"
} >"$TMP"
curl -sS -X POST "$API/api/WorkOrder" \
  -H "Authorization: $TOKEN" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) Chrome/120.0.0.0 Safari/537.36" \
  -H "Origin: $ORIGIN" -H "Referer: ${ORIGIN}/" \
  -H "Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=$BOUNDARY" \
  --data-binary "@$TMP"
rm -f "$TMP"
```

## Resolve numeric `workOrderId` and resident UUID

After create, read **`jobToken`** from the POST JSON (`data.jobToken`).

1. **`GET {API}/api/WorkOrder/{jobToken}`** with the same auth/browser headers.
2. Numeric id: **`data.jobs[0].workOrderId`** (prefer the job row whose token matches `jobToken` if multiple).
3. Full row / resident paths: **`GET {API}/api/WorkOrder/ById/{workOrderId}`** — use **`data.aiResidentComData.resident.userId`** or **`data.location.locationAssignments[0].userId`** for **`ResidentUserId`** (not top-level **`data.userId`** for staff/creator).

## Required reply to the user (no secrets)

Include a compact summary:

- **API base** used  
- **`jobToken`** and **workspace-style URL** if helpful: `{MARKETPLACE_URL}/workspace?request-id={jobToken}` (adjust if your tenant differs)  
- **`workOrderId`**, **`woNumber`**, **`clientId`**, **`locationId`**, **resident UUID** (from `ById`), **`scopeOfWorkSummary`** snippet if relevant  

**Do not** print JWTs or full env dumps.

## Scope and alternatives

- **In scope:** create WO + return identifiers for later RabbitMQ / Roo / scripts.
- **Out of scope:** creating clients, residents, or locations; use **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-client.mdc`**, **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-resident.mdc`**, and **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-location.mdc`** first when needed. **Start Resiroo** / **`ForceResiroo`** / waiting for triage remain in **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/resiroo/y-create-work-order-in-marketplace.mdc`** for UI-heavy flows.
- **`POST /api/WorkOrder/Submit`** + **`PublicWorkOrderSubmissionDto`** is for **public** submission flows (`submissionMethod`, `clientToken`, etc.)—not the workspace **Staff** create validated here.
- **Natural resident email follow-up** (SMTP send, inbox assignment to WO) is handled by **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-mp-email-routing.mdc`** to avoid duplicating routing steps in this rule.
- For full ResiRoo E2E scenarios (WO + resident message + reporting), use **`.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-e2e-resiroo.mdc`** as the orchestration rule.
- For newly created WOs that will be used in resident/Resiroo conversation, start Resiroo before SMTP conversation steps (preferred API: **`POST /api/WorkOrder/ForceResiroo/{jobToken}`**; UI **Start Resiroo Manually** is fallback).

## If `POST /api/WorkOrder` fails

- **403** on API: add/fix **`User-Agent`**, **`Origin`**, **`Referer`**; refresh **`MARKETPLACE_JWT`**.
- **400 / 422 / 500** with validation: compare your JSON to **`WorkOrderCreateDto`** in Swagger; confirm **`locationId`** belongs to **`clientId`**.
- If the contract changes, re-check **`POST /api/WorkOrder`** in the live Swagger and re-run one **multipart** test in a throwaway shell (never log secrets).
